      "errorMessage": "<task id=\"ses_f0768fb56ffeYha706eEqe9mcC\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have gathered comprehensive findings. Here is the full report.\n\n---\n\n# 1. The `a2e-documents` app\n\n**Location:** `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents`\n\nThis is the app whose display name is **Bureau** (`a2e-documents` is the package name; Bureau is the product identity).\n\n### Application config / manifest\n`.../a2e-documents/src/application.config.ts`:\n```ts\nimport { defineApplication } from 'twenty-sdk/define';\n\nexport const APPLICATION_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIER =\n  '19126a9c-7cc0-4368-aaba-c7e5a87b0c48';\n\nexport default defineApplication({\n  universalIdentifier: APPLICATION_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIER,\n  displayName: 'Bureau',\n  description:\n    'Bureau — pages et notes : arborescence de documents, éditeur riche, modèles et partage',\n});\n```\nBuilt manifest: `.../a2e-documents/.twenty/output/manifest.json` (1139 lines). Key registered artifacts:\n- `document` object `c31a0100-0000-4000-8000-000000000000` (manifest lines 18–276), plus `documentCommentThread`, `documentRevision`, `documentFavorite`, `documentMention`.\n- Logic functions (manifest lines 630–846): `post-install`, `purge-archived-documents`, `guard-document-parent-cycle`, `document-content`, `guard-document-revision-save`, `summarize-document`, `translate-document`, `improve-document-writing`, `list-template-descriptors`, `apply-template`, `index-document-mentions`.\n- Front components (lines 847–914): `document-browser`, `document-page`, `create-document-command`, `save-company-as-document-command`, `save-person-as-document-command`, `save-document-as-template-command`.\n- Views (lines 916–1005): `Tous les documents` (TABLE, `openRecordIn: SIDE_PANEL`), `Modèles` (LIST, `kind = TEMPLATE`, `SIDE_PANEL`).\n- Page layout `Document Record Page` (lines 1025–1086).\n- Navigation: `Pages` view row nested under folder `Bureau` (lines 1007–1024).\n\n### Source structure\n```\nsrc/\n├── application.config.ts\n├── command-menu-items/        (create-document, create-document-and-open, go-to-documents, save-*-as-document, save-document-as-template)\n├── constants/                 (universal-identifiers.ts, field-vocabulary.ts)\n├── fields/                    (person/company documents, chrome fields, templateApplyOperationId)\n├── front-components/          (document-browser, document-page, create-document-command, save-* command factory/components)\n├── lib/                       (apply-template, document-template-descriptors, instantiate-template, starter-templates, template-gallery, document-tree, …)\n├── logic-functions/           (apply-template, list-template-descriptors, document-content, translate-document, …)\n├── navigation-menu-items/     (documents.navigation-menu-item.ts, bureau-folder.navigation-menu-item.ts)\n├── objects/                   (document, document-mention, document-favorite, document-revision, document-comment-thread)\n├── page-layouts/              (document.page-layout.ts)\n├── roles/                     (default-function.role.ts)\n└── views/                     (all-documents.view.ts, templates.view.ts)\n```\n\n### The logic functions you asked about\n\n**`apply-template`** — `src/logic-functions/apply-template.ts` (whole file, 50 lines):\n```ts\nconst handler = async (payload: ApplyTemplateRequest) =>\n  applyDocumentTemplateByKey(\n    new CoreApiClient(),\n    {\n      key: typeof payload?.key === 'string' ? payload.key : '',\n      inputs: payload?.inputs ?? null,\n      operationId: payload?.operationId ?? null,\n    },\n    { getInstalledApplications: readInstalledApplications },\n  );\n\nexport default defineLogicFunction({\n  universalIdentifier: LOGIC_FUNCTION_IDS.applyTemplate,   // c31a0000-0012-...000a\n  name: 'apply-template',\n  description: 'Applique un modèle de page listé par A2E Documents …',\n  timeoutSeconds: 120,\n  handler,\n});\n```\n- `readInstalledApplications` (lines 19–30) queries `MetadataApiClient.findManyApplications` for `{name, universalIdentifier}`.\n- `LOGIC_FUNCTION_IDS` in `src/constants/universal-identifiers.ts:68-84`.\n\n**`list-template-descriptors`** — `src/logic-functions/list-template-descriptors.ts` (whole file, 23 lines):\n```ts\nconst handler = async () => ({\n  templates: buildDocumentTemplateDescriptors(),\n});\n\nexport default defineLogicFunction({\n  universalIdentifier: LOGIC_FUNCTION_IDS.listTemplateDescriptors,\n  name: 'list-template-descriptors',\n  description: 'Liste les modèles de pages fournis par A2E Documents …',\n  timeoutSeconds: 30,\n  handler,\n});\n```\n\n**`create-document`** is not a logic function; it is a **front component**:\n`src/front-components/create-document-command.front-component.tsx` (full file, 66 lines) — see section 4 below.\n\n**`daily-note`** is not a logic function or a standalone file. It is a **starter template descriptor** — see section 2. The \"daily note\" affordance (Agenda day header) is the still-unimplemented PLAN **M8e** slice (see section 4 note).\n\nAlso relevant logic functions: `document-content.logic-function.ts`, `translate-document.logic-function.ts`, `summarize-document.logic-function.ts`, `improve-document-writing.logic-function.ts`, `guard-document-parent-cycle.ts`, `guard-document-revision-save.ts`, `index-document-mentions.ts`, `purge-archived-documents.ts`, `post-install.ts`.\n\n---\n\n# 2. M9c Bureau pages template family — descriptor definition\n\nThe \"Bureau pages\" family is a **projection of `STARTER_DOCUMENT_TEMPLATES`** onto the shared C1 descriptor contract. There is no separate descriptor array authoring the family; descriptors are built dynamically.\n\n### The raw family (including the daily note)\n`.../a2e-documents/src/lib/starter-templates.ts` — 20 templates. The daily-note member, lines 42–46:\n```ts\n{\n  title: 'Modèle — Note quotidienne',\n  markdown:\n    '# Note quotidienne\\n\\n## Date\\n\\n## Priorités du jour\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n## Idées\\n\\n## Demain\\n',\n},\n```\nThe other 19 titles are at lines 12–111 (`Notes de réunion`, `Brief de projet`, `Spécifications produit (PRD)`, `Entretien individuel`, `Journal`, `Revue hebdomadaire`, `OKR`, `Accueil du wiki d’équipe`, `Guide d’intégration`, `Ordre du jour récurrent`, `Journal de décisions (ADR)`, `Rétrospective`, `Brainstorming`, `Liste de lecture`, `Notes de cours (Cornell)`, `Plan de thèse`, `Recettes de cuisine`, `Plan de voyage`, `CRM personnel`).\n\n### The descriptor projection\n`.../a2e-documents/src/lib/document-template-descriptors.ts` (whole file, 92 lines). Key parts:\n\n```ts\n// line 16\nexport const DOCUMENTS_TEMPLATE_CATEGORY = 'Pages';\n\n// line 19\nexport const DOCUMENTS_REQUIRED_APPS: string[] = [];\n\n// lines 24-45 — English labels by slug\nconst DOCUMENT_TEMPLATE_EN_LABELS: Record<string, string> = {\n  ...\n  'note-quotidienne': 'Daily note',   // line 31\n  ...\n};\n\n// lines 50-61 — key = slug of the French title minus \"Modèle — \"\nexport const toDocumentTemplateKey = (title: string): string => {\n  const withoutPrefix = title.replace(/^Modèle — /, '');\n  const slug = withoutPrefix\n    .normalize('NFD').replace(/[\\u0300-\\u036f]/g, '')\n    .toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').replace(/^-+|-+$/g, '');\n  return slug.length > 0 ? slug : 'modele';\n};\n\n// lines 63-73 — preview: exactly one document row\nconst DOCUMENT_PREVIEW = [\n  {\n    object: 'document',\n    summary: {\n      fr: 'Crée une page à partir du modèle.',\n      en: 'Creates a page from the template.',\n    },\n    count: 1,\n  },\n];\n\n// lines 75-92 — the actual emitted descriptor\nexport const buildDocumentTemplateDescriptors = (): TemplateDescriptor[] =>\n  STARTER_DOCUMENT_TEMPLATES.map((starterTemplate) => {\n    const key = toDocumentTemplateKey(starterTemplate.title);\n    const frenchLabel = starterTemplate.title.replace(/^Modèle — /, '');\n\n    return {\n      key,\n      version: 1,\n      labels: {\n        fr: frenchLabel,\n        en: DOCUMENT_TEMPLATE_EN_LABELS[key] ?? frenchLabel,\n      },\n      category: DOCUMENTS_TEMPLATE_CATEGORY,   // 'Pages'\n      preview: DOCUMENT_PREVIEW,\n      requiredApps: DOCUMENTS_REQUIRED_APPS,   // []\n      inputs: [],                              // page templates have no user-filled fields\n    };\n  });\n```\n\n### Concrete emitted descriptor for the daily note\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| `key` | `note-quotidienne` |\n| `version` | `1` |\n| `labels.fr` | `Note quotidienne` |\n| `labels.en` | `Daily note` |\n| `category` | `Pages` |\n| `preview` | `[{ object: 'document', summary: { fr: 'Crée une page à partir du modèle.', en: 'Creates a page from the template.' }, count: 1 }]` |\n| `requiredApps` | `[]` |\n| `inputs` | `[]` |\n\nTests asserting this family: `src/lib/__tests__/document-template-descriptors.test.ts` and `src/lib/__tests__/starter-templates.test.ts` (line 20 and 112 assert `'Modèle — Note quotidienne'`).\n\nThe shared contract type `TemplateDescriptor` lives in `packages/twenty-shared/src/application/` (`isTemplateDescriptor`, `validateTemplateDescriptors`).\n\n---\n\n# 3. US-131 \"apply\" path — how the front end invokes `apply-template`\n\nThere are **two functions with the well-known names**, discovered on installed apps:\n- descriptor source = `list-template-descriptors` (US-117)\n- apply = `apply-template` (US-131 / wired by US-132)\n\n### Constants\n`.../twenty-front/src/modules/template-gallery/constants/TemplateApplyLogicFunctionName.ts`:\n```ts\nexport const TEMPLATE_APPLY_LOGIC_FUNCTION_NAME = 'apply-template';\n```\n`.../constants/TemplateDescriptorLogicFunctionName.ts`:\n```ts\nexport const TEMPLATE_DESCRIPTOR_LOGIC_FUNCTION_NAME = 'list-template-descriptors';\n```\n\n### `collectTemplateDescriptorLogicFunctions`\n`.../template-gallery/utils/collectTemplateDescriptorLogicFunctions.ts` (whole file, 45 lines):\n```ts\nexport const collectTemplateDescriptorLogicFunctions = ({\n  logicFunctions,\n  applications,\n}: { logicFunctions: LogicFunction[]; applications: FlatApplication[]; }): TemplateDescriptorLogicFunctionTarget[] => {\n  const applicationsById = new Map(\n    applications.map((application) => [application.id, application]),\n  );\n\n  return logicFunctions.flatMap((logicFunction) => {\n    if (logicFunction.name !== TEMPLATE_DESCRIPTOR_LOGIC_FUNCTION_NAME) return [];\n    if (!isNonEmptyString(logicFunction.applicationId)) return [];\n    const application = applicationsById.get(logicFunction.applicationId);\n    if (!isDefined(application)) return [];\n    return [{ application, logicFunctionId: logicFunction.id }];\n  });\n};\n```\n\n### `ExecuteOneLogicFunction`\n- GraphQL mutation: `.../modules/logic-functions/graphql/mutations/executeOneLogicFunction.ts`:\n```graphql\nmutation ExecuteOneLogicFunction($input: ExecuteOneLogicFunctionInput!) {\n  executeOneLogicFunction(input: $input) { data logs duration status error }\n}\n```\n- Generated types: `.../generated-metadata/graphql.ts:8055-8060`.\n- There is also a generic test hook `.../modules/logic-functions/hooks/useExecuteLogicFunction.ts` (`ExecuteOneLogicFunctionInput = { id, payload }`, lines 11–39). But the gallery does **not** use it; it calls the mutation directly.\n\n### `useTemplateGalleryItems` (list call)\n`.../template-gallery/hooks/useTemplateGalleryItems.ts` (126 lines). It resolves the descriptor targets and, per target, executes:\n```ts\nconst result = await executeOneLogicFunction({\n  variables: { input: { id: target.logicFunctionId, payload: {} } },\n});\nconst templates = extractTemplateDescriptors(result.data?.executeOneLogicFunction?.data);\ngroups.push({\n  applicationUniversalIdentifier: target.application.universalIdentifier,\n  applicationName: target.application.name,\n  templates,\n});\n```\n(lines 42–79; `extractTemplateDescriptors` filters via `isTemplateDescriptor`, lines 114–126.)\n\n### `useApplyTemplate` (the apply call — US-131 write path)\n`.../template-gallery/hooks/useApplyTemplate.ts` (whole file, 109 lines). The essential part:\n```ts\nexport const useApplyTemplate = () => {\n  const applications = useAtomStateValue(applicationsSelector);\n  const logicFunctions = useAtomStateValue(logicFunctionsSelector);\n  const [executeOneLogicFunction] =\n    useMutation<ExecuteOneLogicFunctionMutation>(ExecuteOneLogicFunctionDocument);\n  ...\n  const [operationId] = useState(() => uuidv4());     // one id per gallery session\n\n  const targets = useMemo(\n    () => collectTemplateApplyLogicFunctions({ logicFunctions, applications }),\n    [logicFunctions, applications],\n  );\n\n  const applyTemplate = useCallback(\n    async (item: TemplateGalleryItem): Promise<TemplateApplyResult | null> => {\n      if (isDefined(findSynaRecipeDescriptor(item.descriptor.key))) {\n        return applySynaRecipeItem(item.descriptor.key, operationId);\n      }\n      if (isDefined(findAgendaTemplateDescriptor(item.descriptor.key))) {\n        return applyAgendaTemplateItem(item.descriptor.key, operationId);\n      }\n\n      const target = targets.find(\n        (candidate) =>\n          candidate.application.universalIdentifier ===\n          item.sourceApplication.universalIdentifier,\n      );\n      if (!isDefined(target)) return null;\n\n      setIsApplying(true);\n      try {\n        const response = await executeOneLogicFunction({\n          variables: {\n            input: {\n              id: target.logicFunctionId,\n              payload: { key: item.descriptor.key, inputs: null, operationId },\n            },\n          },\n        });\n        const result = response.data?.executeOneLogicFunction?.data;\n        return isTemplateApplyResult(result) ? result : null;   // line 89\n      } catch {\n        return null;\n      } finally {\n        setIsApplying(false);\n      }\n    },\n    [applyAgendaTemplateItem, applySynaRecipeItem, executeOneLogicFunction, operationId, targets],\n  );\n\n  return { applyTemplate, isApplying: isApplying || isApplyingAgendaTemplate || isApplyingSynaRecipe };\n};\n```\n`collectTemplateApplyLogicFunctions` is the mirror of the descriptor collector — `.../utils/collectTemplateApplyLogicFunctions.ts`:\n```ts\nif (logicFunction.name !== TEMPLATE_APPLY_LOGIC_FUNCTION_NAME) return [];   // 'apply-template'\n...\nreturn [{ application, logicFunctionId: logicFunction.id }];\n```\n\n### `isTemplateApplyResult` (shared contract)\n`packages/twenty-shared/src/application/templateApplyGuards.ts:76-79`:\n```ts\nexport const isTemplateApplyResult = (\n  value: unknown,\n): value is TemplateApplyResult =>\n  isTemplateApplyApplied(value) || isTemplateApplyRejected(value);\n```\n- `isTemplateApplyApplied` (lines 40–57) requires `status === 'applied'`, non-empty `key`, numeric `version`, nullable/string `operationId`, and an array of `{object,id}` records.\n- `isTemplateApplyRejected` (lines 59–74) requires `status === 'rejected'`, non-empty `key`, one of the closed `TemplateApplyErrorCode`s, and a non-empty `message`.\n- `resolveTemplateApplyRequestError` (lines 100–139) is the shared pre-write validator (missing required app / missing input).\n- Types: `packages/twenty-shared/src/application/templateApplyType.ts` (`TemplateApplyResult`, `TemplateApplyErrorCode = UNKNOWN_TEMPLATE_KEY | MISSING_REQUIRED_APP | MISSING_INPUT | APPLY_FAILED`, `TemplateApplyCreatedRecord`, `TemplateApplyInstalledApplications`).\n- Re-exported from `packages/twenty-shared/src/application/index.ts:189,197`.\n\n### The host surface that calls `applyTemplate`\n`.../template-gallery/components/TemplateGallerySidePanelPage.tsx` (82 lines):\n```ts\nconst { applyTemplate, isApplying } = useApplyTemplate();\n\nconst handleUseTemplate = async (item: TemplateGalleryItem) => {\n  setRejection(null);\n  const result = await applyTemplate(item);\n  if (isDefined(result) && isTemplateApplyRejected(result)) {\n    setRejection(result);\n  }\n};\n\n// Blank creation is M13a's create chooser … until it lands the host simply closes\nconst handleBlank = () => { goBackFromSidePanel(); };\n```\nRendered by `TemplateGallery` (`.../components/TemplateGallery.tsx:342-356` — `Use template` / `Blank` buttons). Registered in the side panel via `.../side-panel/constants/SidePanelPagesConfig.tsx:115`.\n\n**Important:** `handleUseTemplate` only applies and renders a rejection. It does **not** open the newly created document. The app's `apply-template` returns the created record id (`apply-template.ts` → `createDocumentFromTemplate`) but the gallery currently ignores `created` for navigation. Anyone implementing M8e/US-146 would need to add the open step.\n\n### The app-side apply implementation\n`.../a2e-documents/src/lib/apply-template.ts` (215 lines). Core write at lines 87–120:\n```ts\nconst payload = buildTemplateCopyPayload({\n  title: starterTemplate.title,\n  content: { markdown: starterTemplate.markdown },\n});\n\nconst result = await client.mutation({\n  createDocuments: {\n    __args: {\n      data: [{\n        title: payload.title,\n        kind: payload.kind,\n        position: payload.position,\n        content: payload.content,\n        ...(operationId === null ? {} : { templateApplyOperationId: operationId }),\n      }],\n    },\n    id: true,\n  },\n});\n```\nIdempotency: `findDocumentIdByOperationId` (lines 70–85) filters `templateApplyOperationId eq operationId` before writing. `buildTemplateCopyPayload` lives in `src/lib/instantiate-template.ts:195-206` and strips `Modèle — ` (→ \"Note quotidienne\") while re-keying blocknote block anchors.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Untitled document creation from the front end\n\nThere is **no native document module in `twenty-front`** — the `document` object is owned by the `a2e-documents` app. I searched `twenty-front/src` for `useCreateDocument`, `createDocument`, `Untitled`, `Sans titre`, `Nouveau document`, `New page`, `Inbox`, `personal root` — no document-specific creation hook or \"Inbox\" concept exists there.\n\n### The canonical app-side creation path\n`.../a2e-documents/src/front-components/create-document-command.front-component.tsx` (whole file, 66 lines) is the canonical create-and-open:\n```ts\nconst CreateDocumentCommand = ({ title }: CreateDocumentCommandParams = {}) => {\n  const execute = async (): Promise<void> => {\n    const client = new CoreApiClient();\n\n    const result = await client.mutation({\n      createDocuments: {\n        __args: {\n          data: [{\n            title: title ?? 'Nouveau document',\n            position: buildAppendPosition(undefined),\n          }],\n        },\n        id: true,\n      },\n    } as never);\n\n    const created = (result as { createDocuments?: { id?: string }[] })\n      .createDocuments?.[0];\n    if (created?.id === undefined) return;\n\n    await navigate(AppPath.RecordShowPage, {\n      objectNameSingular: 'document',\n      objectRecordId: created.id,\n    });\n  };\n\n  return <Command execute={execute} />;\n};\n```\nNotes:\n- Default title is **`'Nouveau document'`** (French), not \"Untitled\".\n- No `parentId` → the record is a **root** of the shared document tree (`parent IS NULL`, see `document-browser` filter at line 147: `{ parent: { id: { is: 'NULL' } } }`).\n- Position is `buildAppendPosition(undefined)` — the fractional append key (`src/lib/fractional-position.ts:221-222`).\n- `kind` defaults to `'DOCUMENT'` on the object (`document.object.ts:59`, manifest line 51).\n- Registered as front component `c31a0000-0013-...0003`; command-menu item `create-document-and-open` (`src/command-menu-items/create-document-and-open.command-menu-item.ts`). There is also `create-document.command-menu-item.ts` which pins `isPinned: true` and opens the **browser**, not a create.\n\n### The app's in-tree create (same title default)\n`.../front-components/document-browser.front-component.tsx:531-558`:\n```ts\nconst createChild = async (parentDocumentId: string | null): Promise<void> => {\n  const client = new CoreApiClient();\n  await client.mutation({\n    createDocuments: {\n      __args: {\n        data: [{\n          title: 'Nouveau document',\n          ...(parentDocumentId === null\n            ? { position: buildAppendPosition(lastRootPosition(documents)) }\n            : {\n                parentId: parentDocumentId,\n                position: buildAppendPosition(lastChildPosition(documents, parentDocumentId)),\n              }),\n        }],\n      },\n      id: true,\n    },\n  } as never);\n  await reloadTree();\n};\n```\nThe `+ Nouveau` button calls `createChild(null)` (lines 757–763); the per-node `+ sous-document` calls `createChild(id)` (lines 1410–1416).\n\n### The host/front-end generic primitives (what a new \"New page\" would use)\nThere is no document wrapper, but the generic record-creation path is:\n- `.../modules/object-record/hooks/useCreateOneRecord.ts` — `useCreateOneRecord({ objectNameSingular: 'document' })`, returns `createOneRecord(recordInput)`. Optimistic cache + Apollo mutation (lines 84–219).\n- `.../modules/object-record/record-table/hooks/useCreateNewIndexRecord.ts` — the \"New record\" command path; creates then opens (see section 5).\n\nClosest existing analog (not document): `.../modules/quick-capture/hooks/useQuickCapture.ts` + `utils/quickCapture.ts` handles Note/Task only; `buildQuickCaptureCreatePlan` returns `recordInput: { title }` and navigates to `AppPath.RecordShowPage`. It has no document target.\n\n### About \"Untitled in Inbox/personal root\"\nThat phrasing comes from **PLAN M8e**, not from implemented code. `PLAN.md:370-372` and `tasks/prd-batch-a.json:304-317`:\n> \"Global shortcut (Cmd+Shift+N) and Cmd+K 'New page' creating an untitled doc in Inbox/personal root; opt-in daily note (template from M9) opened from Agenda day header.\"\n> \"Opt-in daily note: Agenda day header … instantiates the existing daily-note template (M9c Bureau pages: 'daily note ✔') for that date through the US-131 apply path — one note per date (idempotent re-open).\"\n\n`docs/plan/phases/phase-13-report.md:728` shows `US-146/quick-capture-daily-note` was **claimed** by an executor on 2026-10-01 (working tree currently on `main`, no new quick-capture/daily-note module present). So today there is **no** \"Untitled\" title default, **no** \"Inbox\" parent, and **no** Cmd+Shift+N handler. The existing canonical root creation is the `'Nouveau document'` record with no `parent`. `root === parent IS NULL` is the current meaning of \"personal root\".\n\n---\n\n# 5. How documents are opened after creation\n\n### App-side (front components in the sandbox)\nTwo patterns exist:\n\n**(a) Full-page navigation** — `navigate(AppPath.RecordShowPage, { objectNameSingular: 'document', objectRecordId })`. Used by:\n- `create-document-command.front-component.tsx:51-54`\n- `document-browser.front-component.tsx:120-126` (`openDocument`)\n- `document-page.front-component.tsx:122-128` (`openDocument`) and `:446-449` (after creating a child/template copy)\n- `save-record-as-document-command.factory.tsx:122`\n\n**(b) Side panel from the app** — `openSidePanelPage` imported from `twenty-sdk/front-component`:\n`.../document-page.front-component.tsx:130-136`:\n```ts\nconst openDocumentInSidePanel = (documentId: string): void => {\n  void openSidePanelPage({\n    page: SidePanelPages.ViewRecord,\n    recordId: documentId,\n    objectNameSingular: 'document',\n  });\n};\n```\nUsed at line 811 to open child pages.\n\n### Host-side (`twenty-front`) — the canonical open hooks\n`.../modules/side-panel/hooks/useOpenRecordInSidePanel.ts` (213 lines) is the central primitive:\n```ts\nconst openRecordInSidePanel = useCallback(\n  ({ recordId, objectNameSingular, tab, isNewRecord = false,\n     resetNavigationStack = false, openInTab = false }) => {\n    if (isMobile) { /* navigate main outlet to RecordShowPage */ }\n\n    const recordPath = getAppPath(AppPath.RecordShowPage, {\n      objectNameSingular, objectRecordId: recordId,\n    });\n    ...\n    const pageComponentInstanceId = openRoutedPageInSidePanel({\n      path: recordPathWithTab,\n      pageTitle: isNewRecord ? t`New ${objectMetadataItem.labelSingular}` : undefined,\n      resetNavigationStack,\n    });\n\n    if (isNewRecord) {\n      const labelIdentifierField = getLabelIdentifierFieldMetadataItem(objectMetadataItem);\n      if (isDefined(labelIdentifierField)) {\n        openNewRecordTitleCell({ recordId, fieldName: labelIdentifierField.name });\n      }\n    }\n    return pageComponentInstanceId;\n  }, [...]);\n```\n\nThe choice between side panel and full page comes from `.../record-index/hooks/useResolveOpenRecordIn.ts` + `.../record-index/utils/resolveOpenRecordIn.ts` (workspace-member preference + object/v `openRecordIn`). The app's views set `openRecordIn: SIDE_PANEL` (`src/views/all-documents.view.ts:33`, `src/views/templates.view.ts:37`, manifest lines 924/970). The default preference is `SIDE_PANEL` (`.../record-index/constants/DefaultOpenRecordInPreference.ts:3`).\n\n`useCreateNewIndexRecord` (the \"New record\" command) shows the combined create+open decision — `.../record-table/hooks/useCreateNewIndexRecord.ts:79-125`:\n```ts\nconst createdRecord = await createOneRecord({ id: recordId, ...mergedRecordInput });\n\nif (workspaceSurface.type === 'side-panel') {\n  openRecordInSidePanel({ recordId, objectNameSingular, isNewRecord: true, resetNavigationStack: false });\n} else if (openRecordIn === OpenRecordIn.SIDE_PANEL) {\n  openRecordInSidePanel({ recordId, objectNameSingular, isNewRecord: true });\n} else {\n  // open the title cell for typing, then navigate the main outlet\n  store.set(newRecordTitleCellToOpenState.atom, { recordId, fieldName: ... });\n  closeSidePanelMenu();\n  navigate(AppPath.RecordShowPage, { objectNameSingular, objectRecordId: recordId });\n}\n```\nThe same pattern is in `.../record-index/hooks/useOpenRecordFromIndexView.ts:46-133`.\n\n**There is no `openRecordInCommandMenu` / `useOpenRecordInCommandMenu` in this repo.** The template-gallery opens a *page*, not a record:\n`.../template-gallery/hooks/useOpenTemplateGallery.ts:14-34`:\n```ts\nexport const useOpenTemplateGallery = () => {\n  const { navigateSidePanelMenu } = useSidePanelMenu();\n  const store = useStore();\n\n  const openTemplateGallery = ({ category = null } = {}) => {\n    store.set(templateGalleryCategoryPreselectState.atom, category);\n    navigateSidePanelMenu({\n      page: SidePanelPages.TemplateGallery,\n      pageTitle: t`Templates`,\n      pageIcon: IconFileText,\n      resetNavigationStack: true,\n    });\n  };\n  return { openTemplateGallery };\n};\n```\n\n### Gap to note for a \"create document then open it\" feature\n- The app's `apply-template` **does** return `created: [{ object: 'document', id }]` (type `TemplateApplyCreatedRecord`, `twenty-shared/.../templateApplyType.ts:21-24`; populated in `apply-template.ts:116-119, 182-188`).\n- But `TemplateGallerySidePanelPage.handleUseTemplate` (`.../TemplateGallerySidePanelPage.tsx:49-57`) only stores a rejection and never opens the created document. So after a US-131 apply, nothing navigates. Implementing the M8e/agenda/daily-note open behavior means either:\n  1. consuming `result.created[0].id` in the gallery and calling `openRecordInSidePanel({ recordId, objectNameSingular: 'document', isNewRecord: true })` (host), or\n  2. delegating to the app front component / `navigate(AppPath.RecordShowPage, …)`.\n\n---\n\n## Summary of key absolute paths\n- App root: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents`\n- Descriptor family: `.../a2e-documents/src/lib/document-template-descriptors.ts`\n- Starter content (daily note): `.../a2e-documents/src/lib/starter-templates.ts:42-46`\n- Apply lib: `.../a2e-documents/src/lib/apply-template.ts`; wrapper `.../src/logic-functions/apply-template.ts`\n- Create component: `.../a2e-documents/src/front-components/create-document-command.front-component.tsx`\n- Open helpers: `.../src/front-components/document-page.front-component.tsx:122-136`\n- Descriptor collector: `.../twenty-front/src/modules/template-gallery/utils/collectTemplateDescriptorLogicFunctions.ts`\n- Apply collector + hook: `.../utils/collectTemplateApplyLogicFunctions.ts`, `.../hooks/useApplyTemplate.ts`\n- List hook: `.../hooks/useTemplateGalleryItems.ts`\n- Shared guards: `.../twenty-shared/src/application/templateApplyGuards.ts` and `templateApplyType.ts`\n- Open record: `.../twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/hooks/useOpenRecordInSidePanel.ts`\n- Create record: `.../twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/hooks/useCreateOneRecord.ts`; `.../record-table/hooks/useCreateNewIndexRecord.ts`\n- Gallery open seam: `.../template-gallery/hooks/useOpenTemplateGallery.ts`; surface `.../components/TemplateGallerySidePanelPage.tsx`; registered at `.../side-panel/constants/SidePanelPagesConfig.tsx:115`\n\nI did not modify any files.\n</task_result>\n</task>",
