      "result": "<task id=\"ses_f0768fb9dffen1LqXj7YOlvhag\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have completed a thorough exploration. Here is my report.\n\n---\n\n# Cmd+K command menu & global keyboard shortcuts in `packages/twenty-front`\n\n## 1. Where command menu items are defined/registered\n\nThere are **two modules**:\n\n| Module | Path | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `command-menu` | `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu/` | Low-level UI shell + global hotkeys (Cmd+K wiring) |\n| `command-menu-item` | `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu-item/` | Metadata-driven item model, filtering, engine commands, rendering |\n\n### Render chain\n\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ui/layout/page/components/MainAppLayoutWithSidePanel.tsx:47-62` — mounts the hotkeys and the panel:\n```tsx\nexport const MainAppLayoutWithSidePanel = () => {\n  const isMobile = useIsMobile();\n  useCommandMenuHotKeys();                       // line 50\n  return (\n    <StyledRow>\n      ...\n      {isMobile ? <CommandMenuForMobile /> : <SidePanelForDesktop />}  // line 60\n    </StyledRow>\n  );\n};\n```\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu/components/CommandMenuForMobile.tsx:15-33` and `side-panel/components/SidePanelForDesktop.tsx:191` both render `<SidePanelRouter />` inside `CommandMenuOpenContainer` (`command-menu/components/CommandMenuOpenContainer.tsx:44-108`, the styled fixed panel).\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/components/SidePanelRouter.tsx:33-141` resolves the page component from `SIDE_PANEL_PAGES_CONFIG` (lines 61-64) and wraps it in `CommandMenuContextProvider` with `displayType=\"listItem\"` / `containerType={CommandMenuListItem}` (lines 127-134).\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/constants/SidePanelPagesConfig.tsx:47` maps `SidePanelPages.CommandMenuDisplay` → `SidePanelCommandMenuItemDisplayPage`.\n- **The component that renders the list is `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu-item/display/components/SidePanelCommandMenuItemDisplayPage.tsx:28-199`.**\n\n### How items are added — three sources\n\nThere is **no `useCommandMenuItems` hook**. Items come from:\n\n**(a) Server/app metadata items** — `commandMenuItemsSelector` pulls from the metadata store:\n`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu-item/states/commandMenuItemsSelector.ts:8-36`:\n```ts\nexport const commandMenuItemsSelector = createAtomSelector<CommandMenuItemFieldsFragment[]>({\n  key: 'commandMenuItemsSelector',\n  get: ({ get }) => {\n    const commandMenuItems = get(metadataStoreState, 'commandMenuItems').current as FlatCommandMenuItem[];\n    ...\n    return commandMenuItems.filter((item) => item.isActive).map(...)\n  },\n});\n```\nThey are filtered/gated in `command-menu-item/contexts/CommandMenuContextProviderContent.tsx:44-75` (availability type, object metadata id, page type, selection state, page-layout id, `evaluateConditionalAvailabilityExpression`, sorted by `position`).\n\n**(b) Host-hardcoded \"pseudo\" commands** injected directly in `SidePanelCommandMenuItemDisplayPage.tsx` (not metadata):\n```tsx\n// lines 131-141 — selectable ids\nconst selectableItemIds = [\n  ...matchingPinnedItems.map((item) => item.id),\n  ...matchingOtherItems.map((item) => item.id),\n  ...(shouldDisplayQuickCaptureCommand ? [quickCaptureCommandId] : []),\n  ...(shouldDisplayTemplatesCommand ? [templatesCommandId] : []),\n  ...appActions.map((item) => item.id),\n  ...coreObjectsCommandIds,\n  ...\n];\n...\n// lines 160-188 — \"Other\" group\n{shouldDisplayTemplatesCommand && <TemplatesCommand />}\n{shouldDisplayQuickCaptureCommand && <QuickCaptureCommand />}\n{appActions.map(...)}          // from useCommandMenuAppActions\n<CoreObjectsCommands />\n```\n`appActions` come from `command-menu-item/display/hooks/useCommandMenuAppActions.ts:36-58` (toggle drawer, copy link, theme switches). `CoreObjectsCommands` from `object-core/commands/components/CoreObjectsCommands.tsx`. Hooks used: `useTemplatesCommand`, `useQuickCaptureCommand`, `useCoreObjectsCommands`, `useCommandMenuAppActions`.\n\n**(c) Pinned inline buttons** — `command-menu-item/display/components/PinnedCommandMenuItemButtons.tsx:58-72` (filters `commandMenuItems` where `isPinned === true`).\n\nItem shape (`CommandMenuItemFieldsFragment`), from `command-menu-item/graphql/fragments/commandMenuItemFragment.ts:4-33`: `id, universalIdentifier, applicationId, frontComponentId, frontComponent {isHeadless}, engineComponentKey, label, icon, shortLabel, position, isPinned, payload {path}, hotKeys, conditionalAvailabilityExpression, availabilityType, availabilityObjectMetadataId, navigationTargetObjectMetadataId, pageLayoutId, isActive`.\n\nPresentational item: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu/components/CommandMenuItem.tsx:12-79`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Existing documents/pages/notes/templates command entries\n\n### Host \"Templates\" Cmd+K entry (the one relevant to US-132)\n\n`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/template-gallery/components/TemplatesCommand.tsx:13-34` — exact pattern (the QuickCapture pattern):\n```tsx\nexport const TemplatesCommand = () => {\n  const { templatesCommandLabel } = useTemplatesCommand();\n  const { openTemplateGallery } = useOpenTemplateGallery();\n\n  const handleOpenTemplateGallery = () => {\n    openTemplateGallery();\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <SelectableListItem\n      itemId={TEMPLATES_COMMAND_ID}\n      onEnter={handleOpenTemplateGallery}\n    >\n      <CommandMenuItem\n        id={TEMPLATES_COMMAND_ID}\n        label={templatesCommandLabel}\n        Icon={IconFileText}\n        onClick={handleOpenTemplateGallery}\n      />\n    </SelectableListItem>\n  );\n};\n```\n`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/template-gallery/hooks/useTemplatesCommand.ts:6-22` — id/label/search filter:\n```ts\nexport const TEMPLATES_COMMAND_ID = 'templates';\n\nexport const useTemplatesCommand = () => {\n  const sidePanelSearch = useAtomStateValue(sidePanelSearchState);\n  const templatesCommandLabel = t`Templates`;\n  const shouldDisplayTemplatesCommand = normalizeSearchText(\n    templatesCommandLabel,\n  ).includes(normalizeSearchText(sidePanelSearch.trim()));\n  return { templatesCommandId: TEMPLATES_COMMAND_ID, templatesCommandLabel, shouldDisplayTemplatesCommand };\n};\n```\nThe same shape is used by `quick-capture/components/QuickCaptureCommand.tsx:10-27` (id `'quick-capture'`, `IconNotes`).\n\n### App-defined (a2e-*) command menu items — declared in the app lane\n\nDirectory: `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/command-menu-items/`\n\n`create-document.command-menu-item.ts:5-13` (pinned GLOBAL):\n```ts\nexport default defineCommandMenuItem({\n  universalIdentifier: 'c31a0000-0011-4000-8000-000000000001',\n  label: 'Bureau : créer un document',\n  shortLabel: 'Créer un document',\n  availabilityType: 'GLOBAL',\n  isPinned: true,\n  frontComponentUniversalIdentifier: DOCUMENT_BROWSER_FRONT_COMPONENT_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIER,\n});\n```\n`create-document-and-open.command-menu-item.ts:10-16` (GLOBAL, distinct action):\n```ts\nexport default defineCommandMenuItem({\n  universalIdentifier: 'c31a0000-0011-4000-8000-000000000003',\n  label: 'Bureau : créer un document',\n  shortLabel: 'Créer et ouvrir un document',\n  availabilityType: 'GLOBAL',\n  frontComponentUniversalIdentifier: FRONT_COMPONENT_IDS.createDocumentCommand,\n});\n```\n`go-to-documents.command-menu-item.ts:5-12` (`shortLabel: 'Documents'`).\n`save-document-as-template.command-menu-item.ts:15-25` (record-scoped, permission-gated):\n```ts\nexport default defineCommandMenuItem({\n  universalIdentifier: COMMAND_MENU_ITEM_IDS.saveDocumentAsTemplate,\n  label: 'Bureau : enregistrer comme modèle',\n  shortLabel: 'Enregistrer comme modèle',\n  availabilityType: 'RECORD_SELECTION',\n  availabilityObjectUniversalIdentifier: OBJECT_IDS.document,\n  frontComponentUniversalIdentifier: FRONT_COMPONENT_IDS.saveDocumentAsTemplateCommand,\n  conditionalAvailabilityExpression: targetObjectReadPermissions.document,\n});\n```\nOther apps: `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-projects/src/command-menu-items/` (`create-task`, `create-project`, `go-to-projects`, `open-*`, `save-project-as-template`), `a2e-accounting/src/command-menu-items/` (`quick-entry`, `find-subventions`, `save-fiche-as-template`), `a2e-chat/src/command-menu-items/`.\n\n### The exact `defineCommandMenuItem` contract\n\n`packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/command-menu-items/command-menu-item-config.ts:3-8` + `packages/twenty-shared/src/application/frontComponentManifestType.ts:4-14`:\n```ts\nexport type CommandMenuItemManifest = SyncableEntityOptions & {\n  label: string;\n  shortLabel?: string;\n  /** @deprecated icon will be ignored in favor of application icon */\n  icon?: string;\n  isPinned?: boolean;\n  availabilityType?: `${CommandMenuItemAvailabilityType}`;\n  availabilityObjectUniversalIdentifier?: string;\n  frontComponentUniversalIdentifier: string;\n  conditionalAvailabilityExpression?: string;\n};\n```\n`define-command-menu-item.ts:11-29` requires `universalIdentifier`, `label`, `frontComponentUniversalIdentifier`; `icon` is ignored/warns.\n\n> Note on terminology in your request: this codebase does **not** use `onCommandClick` or `shouldBeRegistered`. Click behaviour is either (a) a headless front component using `<Command execute={…} />` — see `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/front-components/create-document-command.front-component.tsx:21-58` — or (b) an `engineComponentKey` handled by `command-menu-item/hooks/useCommandMenuItemClick.ts:68-117`. `hotKeys` exists only as a server column and is rendered by `CommandMenuItemRenderer.tsx:156` (`hotKeys={item.hotKeys}`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Cmd+K and hotkey/hotkey scopes\n\n### Cmd+K\n`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu/hooks/useCommandMenuHotKeys.ts:22-30`:\n```ts\nuseGlobalHotkeys({\n  keys: ['ctrl+k', 'meta+k'],\n  callback: () => {\n    closeKeyboardShortcutMenu();\n    toggleSidePanelMenu();\n  },\n  containsModifier: true,\n  dependencies: [closeKeyboardShortcutMenu, toggleSidePanelMenu],\n});\n```\nSame file also binds `/` → `openRecordsSearchPage` (lines 32-42), `@` → `openAskAiPage` (44-54), and `Escape` on the side panel focus (56-66). It is called once from `MainAppLayoutWithSidePanel.tsx:50`.\n\n`toggleSidePanelMenu` / `openSidePanelMenu` live in `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/hooks/useSidePanelMenu.ts:63-116`; opening navigates to `SidePanelPages.CommandMenuDisplay` with title `Command Menu` (lines 94-99).\n\nThe separate `?` cheat-sheet menu binds its own hotkey in `keyboard-shortcut-menu/components/KeyboardShortcutMenu.tsx:17-25` (`shift+?`, `meta+?`). Its `KeyboardShortcutsGeneral.ts:7-14` lists `Cmd/Ctrl + K` as \"Open search\".\n\n### Hotkey infrastructure / scopes\n- Hook: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ui/utilities/hotkey/hooks/useGlobalHotkeys.ts:16-83` (wraps `react-hotkeys-hook`; defaults: `enableOnContentEditable = true`, `enableOnFormTags = true`, `preventDefault = true`).\n- Gate: `useGlobalHotkeysCallback.ts:33-66` reads `currentGlobalHotkeysConfigSelector` and blocks modifier keys when `enableGlobalHotkeysWithModifiers === false`, and plain keys when `enableGlobalHotkeysConflictingWithKeyboard === false`.\n- Config type/defaults: `types/GlobalHotkeysConfig.ts:1-4`, `constants/DefaultGlobalHotkeysConfig.ts:3-6`.\n- **Scopes are per focus-stack entry**: `globalHotkeysConfig` is passed to `pushFocusItemToFocusStack`. Examples:\n  - Side panel: `side-panel/hooks/useNavigateSidePanel.ts:39-48` (`enableGlobalHotkeysConflictingWithKeyboard: false`).\n  - Keyboard-shortcut menu: `keyboard-shortcut-menu/hooks/useKeyboardShortcutMenu.ts:26-29` (both flags `false`).\n  - Text editors: `blocknote-editor/constants/BlockEditorGlobalHotkeysConfig.ts:1-3`.\n- Focused-element hotkeys: `useHotkeysOnFocusedElement` (used for `Escape`), `HotkeyEffect.tsx`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Install-gating in twenty-front\n\nThere is **no `useIsAppInstalled` / `useInstalledApps` hook by those names.** The actual primitives are:\n\n| Hook/selector | Path | Returns |\n|---|---|---|\n| `applicationsSelector` | `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/applications/states/applicationsSelector.ts:5-12` | `FlatApplication[]` from metadata store (installed apps only) |\n| `useInstalledApplications` | `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/applications/hooks/useInstalledApplications.ts:9-33` | `ApplicationWithoutRelation[]` (metadata apps + `FindManyApplications` logo/registration) |\n| `useA2eSuiteApplications` | `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/a2e-workspace/hooks/useA2eSuiteApplications.ts:15-57` | `{ installedApplications, availableApplications }` |\n| `useIsThirdPartyApplication` | `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/applications/hooks/useIsThirdPartyApplication.ts:16-…` | boolean, by `applicationId` |\n| Known A2E universal IDs | `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/a2e-workspace/constants/A2eSuiteApplicationUniversalIdentifiers.ts:5-18` | `a2e-documents = '19126a9c-7cc0-4368-aaba-c7e5a87b0c48'`, etc. |\n\n**Example usage — the exact install-gate pattern** (`template-gallery/components/TemplateGalleryEntryPoint.tsx:30-44`):\n```tsx\nconst applications = useAtomStateValue(applicationsSelector);\n...\nconst installedUniversalIdentifiers = new Set(\n  applications.map((application) => application.universalIdentifier),\n);\nconst isAvailable = requiredApplicationUniversalIdentifiers.some(\n  (universalIdentifier) => installedUniversalIdentifiers.has(universalIdentifier),\n);\nif (!isAvailable) {\n  return null;\n}\n```\nAnother (per-descriptor `requiredApps`) in `template-gallery/utils/buildTemplateGalleryItems.ts:17-32`:\n```ts\nconst installedApplications = new Set(installedApplicationUniversalIdentifiers);\n...\navailable: descriptor.requiredApps.every((requiredApplication) =>\n  installedApplications.has(requiredApplication),\n),\n```\nAnd app-resolution gating for logic functions in `template-gallery/utils/collectTemplateDescriptorLogicFunctions.ts:24-43` and `collectTemplateApplyLogicFunctions.ts:23-43` (function name must match **and** its `applicationId` must be in the installed set).\n\nInstall/store state is loaded by `applications/components/ApplicationsLoadEffect.tsx:21-121` via `FindManyApplicationsDocument`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. The US-132 \"New\" surface seam (gallery entry points)\n\nCommit: `2b3d7781 agent: US-132 M9a-4: mount gallery entry-points — Cmd+K 'Templates', every 'New' surface, app landing pages`. Report: `docs/plan/phases/phase-13-report.md:444-483`.\n\n### Exports\n\n**`useOpenTemplateGallery`** — the single open seam.\n`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/template-gallery/hooks/useOpenTemplateGallery.ts:14-34`:\n```ts\nexport const useOpenTemplateGallery = () => {\n  const { navigateSidePanelMenu } = useSidePanelMenu();\n  const store = useStore();\n\n  const openTemplateGallery = ({ category = null }: { category?: TemplateDescriptorCategory | null } = {}) => {\n    store.set(templateGalleryCategoryPreselectState.atom, category);\n    navigateSidePanelMenu({\n      page: SidePanelPages.TemplateGallery,\n      pageTitle: t`Templates`,\n      pageIcon: IconFileText,\n      resetNavigationStack: true,\n    });\n  };\n\n  return { openTemplateGallery };\n};\n```\nPreselect atom: `template-gallery/states/templateGalleryCategoryPreselectState.ts:8-12`.\n\n**`TemplateGalleryEntryPoint`** — the exported install-gated \"New\"/\"Use a template\" button.\n`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/template-gallery/components/TemplateGalleryEntryPoint.tsx:24-59`:\n```tsx\nexport const TemplateGalleryEntryPoint = ({\n  requiredApplicationUniversalIdentifiers,\n  category = null,\n  label,\n}: TemplateGalleryEntryPointProps) => {\n  const { t } = useLingui();\n  const applications = useAtomStateValue(applicationsSelector);\n  const { openTemplateGallery } = useOpenTemplateGallery();\n\n  const installedUniversalIdentifiers = new Set(\n    applications.map((application) => application.universalIdentifier),\n  );\n  const isAvailable = requiredApplicationUniversalIdentifiers.some((id) =>\n    installedUniversalIdentifiers.has(id),\n  );\n  if (!isAvailable) { return null; }\n\n  const entryPointLabel = label ?? t`Use a template`;\n  return (\n    <Button\n      Icon={IconFileText}\n      title={entryPointLabel}\n      ariaLabel={entryPointLabel}\n      variant=\"secondary\"\n      size=\"small\"\n      onClick={() => openTemplateGallery({ category })}\n      dataTestId=\"template-gallery-entry-point\"\n    />\n  );\n};\n```\nProps type at `TemplateGalleryEntryPoint.tsx:9-17`: `requiredApplicationUniversalIdentifiers: string[]`, `category?: TemplateDescriptorCategory | null`, `label?: string`.\n\n### How it resolves installed apps\nIt reads `applicationsSelector` and matches `application.universalIdentifier` — the same `flatApplication.universalIdentifier` value that the app declares in its `application.config.ts` (e.g. a2e-documents `'19126a9c-7cc0-4368-aaba-c7e5a87b0c48'`). The gallery data layer resolves descriptors per installed app by the well-known function name `'list-template-descriptors'` (`collectTemplateDescriptorLogicFunctions.ts` + `useTemplateGalleryItems.ts:42-93`), and opens via `'apply-template'` (`useApplyTemplate.ts:46-103` + `TemplateApplyLogicFunctionName.ts:6`).\n\n### Supporting pieces\n- `TemplatesCommand` (Cmd+K) — described in §2.\n- `TemplateGallerySidePanelPage` — `template-gallery/components/TemplateGallerySidePanelPage.tsx:37-82` (the one host surface; `onUseTemplate` → `useApplyTemplate`, renders typed rejection; `onBlank` → back).\n- Registered at `side-panel/constants/SidePanelPagesConfig.tsx:115`.\n- Presentational: `template-gallery/components/TemplateGallery.tsx:191-362` (`Use template` / `Blank`).\n- Enum member: `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/SidePanelPages.ts:48-50` (`TemplateGallery = 'template-gallery'`).\n- Cmd+K list wiring: `SidePanelCommandMenuItemDisplayPage.tsx:13-14, 42-43, 117-123, 134-135, 159-164`.\n\n### Important caveat (from the US-132 report)\nThe report states (`docs/plan/phases/phase-13-report.md:478-483`) that the **concrete a2e-documents app-side \"New\" embedding is deferred** to the L-TPL app lane, and a grep confirms `TemplateGalleryEntryPoint` and `useOpenTemplateGallery` are currently referenced **only by their own tests** (and `TemplatesCommand`) — no production call site outside the template-gallery module yet. The app-side document browser's `+ Nouveau` button (`packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/front-components/document-browser.front-component.tsx:757-763`) creates a document directly and does **not** call `useOpenTemplateGallery`; that app has its own self-contained `Modèles` gallery section at lines 817-832 using `collectGalleryTemplates` (`a2e-documents/src/lib/template-gallery.ts:9-24`). The app-side `create-document` Cmd+K action is `create-document-command.front-component.tsx:21-58`.\n\nSo within `twenty-front`, the US-132 \"New\" seam to reuse is exactly `useOpenTemplateGallery({ category })` or `<TemplateGalleryEntryPoint requiredApplicationUniversalIdentifiers={[…]} category=\"…\" />` — the report explicitly instructs not to add a second open path.\n</task_result>\n</task>"
